<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 343 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 343 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of August 29 raised 343 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 391 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The August 29 issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 71 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.74 (14.74)	    63.5  (75.6)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.95 (16.95)	    85.1 (115.7)</p>
<p>    12 months		 17.85 (17.85)	    77.3 (100.6)</p>
<p>    24 months		 21.76 (21.76)	   117.4  (99.1)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,561 to the U.S. dollar on Monday, from 1,562 last week. It closed at 1,613.5 one year ago.</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602056 645456</p>
</text>
